   "n": "弗 is not simply a variant of 不. It is generally analysed as 不 with the object pronoun 之 fused into it — 'does not ——it' — which is why 居 'settle in' needs no object after it. Not every scholar accepts the fusion, but every reading agrees that an object is understood. 功成 is a whole clause used as the setting for what follows: 'the work being finished, ...'. This line is the hinge of the chapter, and the next unit turns straight back on it."
